    "Older bindings are removed at successful checkpoint; canonical replacement on an already-loaded Engine invalidates target mappings, preserving caller values. Metadata-only replacement keeps continuity.",
    "Invalid continuity shuts down any live adapter before fresh creation; fresh transcript replay retains existing source policy: only canonical user/assistant text from the latest summary boundary, once.",
    "Existing physical workspace/provider checks and owner-changed fork behavior remain adapter-owned. OpenCode forks still create new sessions with history; Codex/Claude native fork paths remain."
